            <ArticleTitle>Deep brain stimulation for the relief of chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Deep brain stimulation analgesia is an effective method of treating otherwise intractable chronic pain, with few side-effects, and long-term good or better results in 50% to 80% of patients, depending on etiology and stimulation site. In general, the best results are in deafferentation pain with internal capsule stimulation and somatic pain with periventricular stimulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
